.\" Manual page for the DistroForge command-line interface.
.\" Every command name, option name, choice list and default documented here is
.\" derived from the argparse parser in distroforge/cli.py and the option
.\" registrations in distroforge/commands/, not written from memory.
.TH distroforge 1 2026-07-26 "DistroForge 0.3.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
distroforge \- plan and build Ubuntu/Debian live ISO images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B distroforge
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
.B distroforge new
.I NAME PROJECT
.RB [ \-\-release
.IR VERSION ]
.RB [ \-\-starter
.IR KEY ]
.PP
.B distroforge plan
.I PROJECT
.PP
.B distroforge readiness
.I PROJECT
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B distroforge build
.I PROJECT
.RI [ BUILD\-OPTIONS ]
.RB [ \-\-execute ]
.PP
.B distroforge iso\-build
.I PROJECT
.RB [ \-\-execute ]
.RB [ \-\-boot\-proof
.IR MODE ]
.PP
.B distroforge gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B distroforge
plans, validates, builds, tests and releases customized Ubuntu and Debian live
ISO images. A DistroForge
.I project
is a host directory holding a
.I project.json
description, a
.I work/
staging area and a
.I dist/
output directory; every command above operates on such a directory.
.PP
The tool is dry\-run first. A build prints and records the command history it
.I would
run and produces no ISO until
.B \-\-execute
is given, and privileged operations go through an explicit privilege helper
selected with
.BR \-\-privilege .
Reviewing commands
.RB ( \fBplan\fR ,
.BR readiness ,
.BR dry\-run\-report ,
.BR explain ,
.BR explain\-risk )
never mutate the host or the image.
.PP
.B distroforge
exposes 84 top\-level commands. Rather than a flat list, they form the coherent
groups below; each command accepts
.B \-\-help
for its own options. The Qt desktop application
.BR distroforge\-gui (1)
covers the same workflows, and
.BR distroforge\-typer (1)
is an optional slim facade over the most common ones.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Catalogs and vocabulary
Read\-only listings of the bundled catalogs, plus the didactic surfaces.
.TP
.BR releases ", " profiles ", " desktops ", " personas ", " presets ", " source\-starters ", " branding\-palettes ", " derivative\-profiles ", " frameworks ", " chroot\-backends ", " autoinstall\-templates
List the corresponding bundled catalog or host capability.
.TP
.BR glossary " [\fITERM\fR]"
Explain DistroForge and ISO\-build vocabulary.
.TP
.BR guided\-recipe " [\fINAME\fR], " recipe " \fITEXT\fR"
List the curated recipe prompts, or expand one into a candidate definition.
.TP
.B build\-phases
Print the per\-phase build contracts (inputs, artifacts, privileges, rollback
points).
.B \-\-stage
scopes the catalog to one pipeline stage.
.SS Creating and describing a project
.TP
.BR new " \fINAME PROJECT\fR, " wizard " \fINAME PROJECT\fR"
Create a project.
.B wizard
is the beginner\-first entry point and defaults
.B \-\-profile
to
.BR portable ;
both accept
.BR "\-\-profile portable|desktop|dev|kiosk" ,
.BR \-\-starter ,
.B \-\-release
and
.BR \-\-plan\-only .
.TP
.BR init\-definition " \fIPATH\fR"
Write an example YAML/JSON image definition.
.TP
.BR profile " {\fBcreate\fR|\fBapply\fR|\fBshow\fR|\fBdiff\fR|\fBresolve\fR}"
Compose package profiles from a base plus repeated
.B \-\-layer
and
.B \-\-override
selections.
.TP
.BR derivative\-profile " {\fBplan\fR|\fBvalidate\fR|\fBexport\fR|\fBcreate\-project\fR}"
Plan or export a downstream derivative distribution profile.
.TP
.BR export\-recipe ", " export\-build\-preset ", " plugins ", " history
Export the project as a reusable recipe or maintainer build preset, list local
plugins, or list and replay local build history.
.SS Reviewing before building
.TP
.BR plan " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Print the ordered build pipeline for the project.
.TP
.BR validate " \fIPROJECT\fR, " compat " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Validate the project, host and option contracts, and check release
compatibility.
.TP
.BR readiness " \fIPROJECT\fR, " dry\-run\-report " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Show the readiness dashboard, or write a structured dry\-run report.
.TP
.BR explain " \fIPROJECT\fR, " explain\-risk " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Explain in plain language what a build would do, and which selected options are
risky.
.B "explain \-\-strict"
promotes advisory findings to blocking ones.
.TP
.BR journey " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Show the guided build journey.
.B \-\-level
selects
.BR beginner ,
.BR power\-user ,
.B maintainer
or
.BR developer ;
.B \-\-apply
and
.B \-\-check
act on a single step.
.TP
.BR ux\-audit " \fIPROJECT\fR, " ai\-review " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Audit persona friction and CLI/GUI parity, or run the local advisory review.
.SS Host readiness
.TP
.BR doctor ", " host ", " iso\-toolchain ", " iso\-doctor " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Report host tooling and build capabilities.
.B doctor \-\-python
checks the Python dependency set,
.B doctor \-\-debian\-dev
audits the Debian/Ubuntu maintainer toolchain, and
.B iso\-toolchain \-\-install
prints and optionally runs the one apt command that installs the missing ISO
tools.
.SS Building
.TP
.BR build " \fIPROJECT\fR"
The full build surface: 191 long options, described under
.B OPTIONS
below. Dry\-run unless
.B \-\-execute
is given.
.TP
.BR iso\-build " \fIPROJECT\fR"
The guarded one\-command ISO path. Without
.B \-\-execute
it stays a dry\-run and writes
.IR dist/ISO\-BUILD.json .
.TP
.BR beginner\-iso " \fIPROJECT\fR, " poweruser\-iso " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Prepare the safe beginner or the guarded power\-user source\-to\-ISO path, with
.BR \-\-apply\-safe\-defaults .
.TP
.BR demo\-iso " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Try the shortest demonstrable ISO path on the current host.
.TP
.BR iso\-accept " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Accept or block a produced ISO for publication.
.TP
.BR restore\-snapshot " \fIPROJECT SNAPSHOT\fR"
Restore a rootfs rollback snapshot.
.SS Branding, debranding and mirrors
.TP
.BR branding " {\fBset\fR|\fBaudit\fR|\fBvalidate\fR|\fBcompliance\fR|\fBclearance\fR|\fBpreview\fR|\fBexport\fR|\fBimport\fR}"
Manage image identity and trademark clearance.
.B \-\-mode
selects
.BR internal ,
.B redistributable
or
.BR approved .
.TP
.BR debrand " {\fBscan\fR|\fBplan\fR|\fBapply\fR}"
Find and remove upstream identity text from a source ISO.
.TP
.BR mirrors " {\fBdoctor\fR|\fBrender\fR|\fBapply\fR|\fBrestore\fR}"
Diagnose and manage the deb822 APT mirror layer.
.SS Capture and alternative image backends
.TP
.BR capture " \fITARGET\fR, " capture\-diff " \fIPROFILE\fR, " rebuild\-from\-capture " \fIPROFILE PROJECT\fR"
Extract a sanitized profile from an installed system, review it, and rebuild
from it. Capture is read\-only and never copies homes, keys, caches or machine
identity.
.TP
.BR live\-build\-plan " \fIPROFILE\fR, " livefs\-iso\-plan " \fIPROFILE\fR, " livefs\-iso\-build " \fIPROFILE\fR"
Render a reviewable Debian live\-build
.I config/
tree, or an Ubuntu livefs ISO workspace.
.TP
.BR upgrade\-media ", " image\-plan
Read\-only upgrade\-media preflight, and OEM/systemd image planning.
.SS Virtualization and boot evidence
.TP
.BR preview " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Plan or launch a drivable preview VM.
.B \-\-display
selects
.BR gtk ,
.B spice
or
.BR none .
.TP
.BR qemu\-interaction " \fIPROJECT\fR, " qemu\-smoke\-plan
Run a declarative QMP interaction plan, or render the live/install smoke
matrix.
.TP
.BR boot\-proof " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Write normalized boot evidence.
.B \-\-backend
selects
.BR auto ,
.B qemu
or
.BR iso\-scan .
.TP
.BR secureboot\-assist " \fIOUTPUT_DIR\fR"
Plan the Secure Boot MOK key workflow.
.SS Release, publication and signing
.TP
.BR artifact\-paths " \fIPROJECT\fR, " release\-readiness ", " release\-gate " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Show host artifact paths, summarize release readiness, and run the maintainer
publication gate.
.TP
.BR publish\-bundle " \fIPROJECT\fR, " sign\-release " \fIPROJECT\fR, " release\-notes " \fIPROJECT\fR, " verify\-release " \fIPROJECT\fR, " explain\-release " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Build the inspection bundle under
.IR dist/publish/ ,
add signing evidence, write notes, verify the bundle and explain its evidence.
.TP
.BR publish\-drill " \fIPROJECT\fR, " publish\-drill\-baseline " \fIPROJECT\fR, " publish\-drill\-diff " \fIOLD NEW\fR, " release\-pipeline " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Rehearse the whole publication sequence, promote a baseline, compare two
drills, or run the pipeline end to end.
.SS Debian packaging evidence
.TP
.BR packaging\-policy " \fIPROJECT\fR, " buildinfo\-report " \fIBUILDINFO\fR, " debian\-package " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Review the packaging policy verdict, inspect
.I .buildinfo
taint, and wrap the maintainer package build.
.TP
.BR autopkgtest\-doctor " \fIPROJECT\fR, " hermetic\-build\-plan " \fIPROJECT\fR, " hermetic\-release\-bundle " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Classify a real autopkgtest run, render the clean\-build plan for
.BR sbuild ,
.B pbuilder
or
.BR mmdebstrap ,
and assemble a local release evidence bundle.
.TP
.BR evidence\-status " \fIPROJECT\fR, " evidence\-verify " \fIPATH\fR, " ci " \fIPROJECT\fR"
Summarize maintainer evidence without building, validate a bundle contract, and
run the lint/test/dry\-run CI plan.
.SS Advisory
.TP
.BR forgeadvisor " {\fBcopilot\fR|\fBexplain\-evidence\fR|\fBfix\-plan\fR|\fBreview\-build\fR|\fBpropose\-fixes\fR|\fBreview\-definition\fR|\fBsearch\-local\fR|\fBexplain\-log\fR|\fBtriage\-log\fR|\fBdoctor\-ai\fR|\fBmemory\fR}"
The local\-first advisory layer. It explains, cites and proposes; it never
builds, signs or applies anything. Every subcommand except
.B memory
accepts
.B \-\-backend
.RB ( offline ,
.BR llama ,
.BR ollama )
and
.B \-\-register
.RB ( beginner ,
.BR power\-user ,
.BR maintainer ,
.BR developer ).
.SS Desktop application
.TP
.B gui
Launch the Qt desktop interface; equivalent to
.BR distroforge\-gui (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option list for
.B distroforge
or for any subcommand and exit.
.SS Conventions shared by many subcommands
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the machine\-readable form of the report instead of the text form. Accepted
by most reporting commands.
.TP
.BI \-\-definition " FILE"
Load an image definition (YAML or JSON) and apply it before command\-line
overrides. Command\-line options win over the definition.
.TP
.B \-\-execute
Leave dry\-run mode and actually run the planned commands. Without it, mutating
commands only record the command history they would have run.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE"
Write the report or generated artifact to
.I FILE
instead of standard output.
.SS Options of distroforge build
.B distroforge build
accepts 191 long options besides
.BR \-\-help .
They are registered in
.I distroforge/commands/build_options.py
and classified in
.I distroforge/commands/build_contracts.py
by user level \(em 27 beginner, 59 power\-user, 77 maintainer and 28 developer
\(em and by the GUI surface that mirrors them. Deliberately, this page does not
reprint them as one wall of flags: the families below are the actual option
groups, and
.B "distroforge build \-\-help"
prints the complete list with every choice and default.
.PP
Every family can say "disabled" cleanly: an unset family costs nothing in the
plan, the dry\-run or the report.
.TP
.B Source selection and trust (9)
.BR \-\-source\-iso ,
.BR \-\-definition ,
.BR \-\-persona ,
.BR \-\-from\-scratch ,
.BR \-\-source\-iso\-sha256 ,
.BR \-\-source\-iso\-signature ,
.BR \-\-source\-iso\-gpg\-fingerprint ,
.BR \-\-require\-source\-iso\-checksum ,
.BR \-\-require\-source\-iso\-signature .
.B \-\-persona
takes
.BR noob ,
.BR friendly ,
.BR intermediate ,
.B pro
or
.BR dev_maintainer .
.TP
.B Bootstrap, when building from scratch (3)
.BR \-\-bootstrap\-arch " (default " amd64 "), "
.BR \-\-bootstrap\-variant " (default " minbase "), "
.BR \-\-bootstrap\-mirror .
A foreign
.B \-\-bootstrap\-arch
requires
.B qemu\-user\-static
on the host.
.TP
.B Packages and package profiles (6)
.BR \-\-install ,
.BR \-\-remove ,
.BR \-\-profile ,
.BR \-\-snap ,
.BR \-\-purge ,
.BR \-\-synaptic .
The first four are repeatable and also accept comma\-separated values.
.TP
.B APT sources, caches, mirrors and PPAs (12)
.BR \-\-mirrors ,
.BR \-\-mirror\-archive ,
.BR \-\-mirror\-security ,
.BR \-\-mirror\-country ,
.BR \-\-mirror\-allow\-http ,
.BR \-\-mirror\-override\-ubuntu\-security ,
.BR \-\-apt\-cache ,
.BR \-\-apt\-cache\-dir ,
.BR \-\-apt\-proxy ,
.BR \-\-apt\-snapshot ,
.BR \-\-ppa ,
.BR \-\-ppa\-no\-auto\-key .
.B \-\-ppa
takes
.BI ppa: owner / name
or
.BI ppa: owner / name @ FINGERPRINT .
.TP
.B Release track (7)
.BR \-\-release\-track " (" stable ", " devel ", " rolling "; default " stable "), "
.BR \-\-devel\-suite ,
.BR \-\-enable\-backports ,
.BR \-\-enable\-proposed ,
.BR \-\-proposed\-pin " (default 100), "
.BR \-\-rolling\-upgrades ,
.BR \-\-rolling\-full\-upgrade .
.TP
.B System sync (6)
.BR \-\-system\-sync ,
.BR \-\-system\-sync\-strategy " (" safe ", " full "; default " full "), "
.BR \-\-system\-sync\-no\-fallback ,
.BR \-\-system\-sync\-hold ,
.BR \-\-system\-sync\-post\-install\-only ,
.BR \-\-system\-sync\-no\-post\-install\-tool .
.TP
.B Desktop, locale and identity (8)
.BR \-\-desktop ,
.BR \-\-display\-manager " (" gdm3 ", " lightdm ", " sddm "), "
.BR \-\-autologin\-user ,
.BR \-\-wallpaper ,
.BR \-\-hostname ,
.BR \-\-locale ,
.BR \-\-timezone ,
.BR \-\-keyboard\-layout .
Run
.B distroforge desktops
for the accepted
.B \-\-desktop
keys.
.TP
.B Users, services, network, kiosk, OEM and drivers (12)
.BR \-\-user ,
.BR \-\-enable\-service ,
.BR \-\-disable\-service ,
.BR \-\-mask\-service ,
.BR \-\-netplan\-dhcp ,
.BR \-\-dns ,
.BR \-\-kiosk ,
.BR \-\-kiosk\-url ,
