.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed. A report command exiting 0 does not mean the report is
clean: read the verdict, which may be
.BR ready ,
.B review
or
.BR blocked .
.TP
.B 1
No command was given, so the top\-level help was printed instead.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or a handled runtime failure: an unknown or misused option
(argparse), a missing file or directory, malformed JSON or YAML, an invalid
option value, or a project that does not exist. The message goes to standard
error as
.RB \(lq distroforge: " error: " \fITEXT\fR \(rq.
.PP
.B distroforge gui
propagates the exit status of the Qt application, which is
.B 2
when no Qt Python bindings are installed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISTROFORGE_PRIVILEGE
Default privilege backend when
.B \-\-privilege
is not given:
.BR sudo " (the default), "
.B pkexec
or
.BR none .
.TP
.B SUDO_ASKPASS
Graphical askpass helper. When set, or when one is detected, privileged
commands use
.B "sudo \-A"
so a build started without a terminal can still authenticate.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base of the host\-owned build\-memory corpus; defaults to
.IR ~/.local/state .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base of the desktop application preferences; defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.BR DISTROFORGE_LLAMA_MODEL ", " DISTROFORGE_OLLAMA_MODEL
Model passed to the optional local advisory backends. Without
.BR DISTROFORGE_LLAMA_MODEL ,
the
.B llama
backend degrades to
.BR offline ;
.B DISTROFORGE_OLLAMA_MODEL
defaults to
.BR llama3 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I PROJECT/project.json
The project description: name, release, source mode, packages and
customization.
.TP
.I PROJECT/work/
Staging area.
.I work/filesystem
is the extracted rootfs and
.I work/iso
the ISO tree; both are permission boundaries written only through the
filesystem\-operations layer.
.I work/snapshots
holds rollback archives.
.TP
.I PROJECT/dist/
Host output directory: the ISO, its
.IR SHA256SUMS ,
.IR BUILDINFO ,
.IR distroforge\-provenance.json ,
the HTML report and the JSON reports
.RI ( ISO\-BUILD.json ,
.IR ISO\-ACCEPTANCE.json ,
.IR RELEASE\-GATE.json ,
.IR PUBLISH\-DRILL.json ,
.IR boot\-proof.json ,
.IR qemu\-lab\-report.json ).
The canonical default ISO name is
.IR dist/ NAME \- VERSION .iso ;
.B \-\-output\-iso
overrides it.
.TP
.I PROJECT/dist/publish/
The maintainer inspection bundle written by
.BR publish\-bundle :
the ISO, release evidence,
.IR RELEASE\-GATE.json ,
.IR RELEASE\-MANIFEST.json ,
.IR SIGNING\-REPORT.json ,
.IR VERIFY\-REPORT.json ,
.IR RELEASE\-NOTES.md ,
.I CHANGELOG.txt
and
.IR README\-PUBLISH.txt .
.TP
.I PROJECT/hooks/
Local shell hooks, run only when the build executes.
.TP
.I PROJECT/plugins/
Local plugins, loaded only when the build executes.
.TP
.I PROJECT/.distroforge/history.jsonl
Project\-owned build history, replayable with
.BR "distroforge history replay" .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/distroforge/build\-memory.jsonl
Host\-owned, append\-only build\-memory corpus, one line per build attempt. It
grounds the advisory citations and is written only when a build actually runs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/distroforge/
Desktop application preferences.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/distroforge/
Installed documentation, and the reviewable example definitions under
.IR examples/ .
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a project and inspect the whole path without touching the host:
.PP
.EX
distroforge releases
distroforge new MyDistro ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \-\-release 26.04
distroforge plan ~/DistroForge/MyDistro
distroforge readiness ~/DistroForge/MyDistro
distroforge dry\-run\-report ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \-\-json
.EE
.PP
Dry\-run a customized build, then execute it explicitly:
.PP
.EX
distroforge build ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \\
    \-\-desktop ubuntu_minimal \-\-install git,curl \-\-locale en_US.UTF\-8
distroforge build ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \\
    \-\-desktop ubuntu_minimal \-\-install git,curl \-\-execute
.EE
.PP
Take the guarded one\-command path and accept the result:
.PP
.EX
distroforge iso\-doctor ~/DistroForge/MyDistro
distroforge iso\-build ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \-\-execute \-\-boot\-proof auto
distroforge iso\-accept ~/DistroForge/MyDistro
.EE
.PP
Enforce source trust and supply\-chain policy:
.PP
.EX
distroforge build ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \\
    \-\-source\-iso ~/iso/source.iso \\
    \-\-source\-iso\-sha256 SHA256 \-\-require\-source\-iso\-checksum \\
    \-\-vuln\-scan \-\-vuln\-policy block\-critical \-\-sbom\-format spdx
.EE
.PP
Capture an installed system as reviewable intent, then rebuild from it:
.PP
.EX
distroforge capture / \-\-output system\-profile.yaml \-\-sanitize strict
distroforge capture\-diff system\-profile.yaml
distroforge rebuild\-from\-capture system\-profile.yaml ~/DistroForge/Rebuilt
.EE
.PP
Rehearse a publication without signing anything:
.PP
.EX
distroforge release\-gate ~/DistroForge/MyDistro
